   <media:title>Two Brothers, Two Maserati | Stories of the Trident, Chapter 1.​</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/snAb8XHxPk8?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/snAb8XHxPk8/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Three Michelin stars. Two brothers. Two ways of experiencing the road.​
Meet Massimiliano and Raffaele Alajmo, the brothers behind Le Calandre restaurant. For Raffaele, his Maserati GranCabrio is a daily ritual, a mix of calm and power. For Massimiliano, his Maserati Grecale is about enjoying the road and letting Grecale inspire his direction.​
This is Chapter 1 of Stories of the Trident, visiting friends of the brand in their own spaces, on their own terms.​
Next in the series: Gary Kao, owner of a bespoke Fuoriserie GT2 Stradale, a stunning tribute to the MC12. ​
Subscribe to be the first to discover the next chapter.​
#Maserati​</media:description>
