  <title>Maserati at the 1000 Miglia 2026. The most beautiful race of the world</title>
  <link rel="alternate" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kV-QrDmVBp4"/>
  <author>
   <name>Maserati</name>
   <uri>https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCrragB5FbqfGKWyXoD-UAEg</uri>
  </author>
  <published>2026-06-18T17:00:05+00:00</published>
  <updated>2026-10-13T20:13:07+00:00</updated>
  <media:group>
   <media:title>Maserati at the 1000 Miglia 2026. The most beautiful race of the world</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/kV-QrDmVBp4?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/kV-QrDmVBp4/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>1,000 miles. 5 days. Infinite emotion.
The 2026 edition of the 1000 Miglia, the most beautiful race in the world, has officially crossed the finish line.

From the starting line in Brescia down to the eternal sunset of Rome and back again, we traced the historic roads of the Bel Paese in a cinematic celebration of performance, design, and pure Italian passion. This journey was more than a race; it was a tribute to our past, present, and the future we are building today.

Watch the full recap video to experience the roar, the breathtaking scenery, and the sheer joy of the drive.

This year’s epic figure-eight route took our fleet across some of Italy's most iconic landscapes and art cities:

Brescia to Padova &amp; Modena: Heading south through the heart of Motor Valley, including a very special homecoming at our HQ in Modena.
The Apennines &amp; Tuscany: Climbing the legendary hairpins of the Passo dell’Abetone, passing through the historic walls of Lucca, Pisa, and the red-brick beauty of Siena.
Rome to the Adriatic Coast: Leaving the Eternal City to head north through the quiet water mirrors of the Comacchio lagoons and the Renaissance streets of Ferrara, before the grand finish back in Brescia.

The Maserati lineup stood at the center of the event:

The 1953 Maserati A6GCS/53 Fantuzzi: A five-time veteran of the original speed race, performing flawlessly on the roads it knows by heart.
The Maserati GranTurismo Trofeo &amp; Maserati GranCabrio Modena: Embodying the peak of modern open-air Grand Touring in special liveries.
This year's 1000 Miglia represents another unforgettable milestone in our &quot;100 Years of the Trident&quot; celebration. It is a testament to the belief that true elegance, craftsmanship, and performance are meant to last.

Which was your favorite moment of the 1000 Miglia 2026? 

Subscribe to the Maserati YouTube Channel for more exclusive stories, product reveals, and behind-the-scenes action.

#Maserati #1000Miglia #MaseratiClassiche #MaseratiGranTurismo #MaseratiGranCabrio #MaseratiFuoriserie</media:description>
